BEGIN_PGML If a temperature is [`50^{\circ}F\text{,}`] what is that temperature in Celsius?
[@KeyboardInstructions('You may use [|degC|]* for [`^{\circ}C\text{.}`]')@]**
[_]{$celsius[0]}{20}
END_PGML
########## # Solution ##########
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION [` \begin{aligned}[t] \frac{5}{9}(\substitute{50} - 32)\amp=\frac{5}{9}(18)\\ \amp=\frac{5}{1}(2)=10 \end{aligned} `]
So [`50^{\circ}F`] is equivalent to [`10^{\circ}C\text{.}`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
