Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML If a temperature is [`-20^{\circ}F\text{,}`] what is that temperature in Celsius?
[@KeyboardInstructions('You may use [|degC|]* for [`^{\circ}Cs\text{.}`]')@]**
[_]{$celsius[1]}{20}
END_PGML
########## # Solution ##########
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION [` \begin{aligned}[t] \frac{5}{9}(\substitute{-20} - 32)\amp=\frac{5}{9}(-52)\\ \amp=-\frac{260}{9}\approx-28.89 \end{aligned} `]
So [`-20^{\circ}F`] is equivalent to about [`-28.89^{\circ}C\text{.}`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
